 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 535274,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the surface area of the octagonal prism shown.<br>\n\n<img src=\"exercises/media/c5d78b22868303c6.png\" alt=\"An octagonal prism. Each side of the octagon measures 4 inches. The height of the prism measures h equals 8 inches. The apothem is marked a equals 5 inches.\">\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"416\\,\\text{in}{^2}\">416\\,\\text{in}{^2}</span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The surface area of a right prism where <i>B</i> is the area of the base, <i>p</i> is the perimeter of the base, and <i>h</i> is the height is <span data-math=\"SA = 2B + ph\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The apothem of a regular polygon is a line segment that starts at the center and is perpendicular to a side. The area of a regular polygon with apothem <i>a</i> and perimeter <i>p</i> is <span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}ap\"></span>.</p>\n<p>A regular octagon has eight sides of equal length. Therefore, the perimeter is:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"p = 8(4{\\text{ in)  =  32 in}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}ap = \\frac{1}{2}\\left( {{\\text{5 in}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{32 in}}} \\right) = 80{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2}\"></span>, which in the surface area formula is <i>B.</i></p>\n<p>The surface area <span data-math=\"= {\\text{ }}2B + ph = {\\text{ }}2\\left( {80{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2}} \\right){\\text{ }} + {\\text{ }}\\left( {32{\\text{ in}}} \\right)\\left( {8{\\text{ in}}} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}160{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2} + {\\text{ }}256{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2} = {\\text{ }}416{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2}\"></span>.\n</p><p>The surface area is 416 square inches.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 535275,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the volume of the octagonal prism shown with the apothem equal to <span data-math=\"5\\,\\text{in},\">5\\,\\text{in},</span> the side length equal to <span data-math=\"4\\,\\text{in},\">4\\,\\text{in},</span> and the height equal to <span data-math=\"8\\,\\text{in}.\">8\\,\\text{in}.</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The volume of a right prism is <span data-math=\"V = Bh\"></span> <span data-math=\"= {\\text{ }}\\left( {80{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{ }}8{\\text{ in}}} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}640{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^3}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The volume is 640 cubic inches.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"640\\,\\text{in}{^3}\">640\\,\\text{in}{^3}</span>"
    }
   ],
